{"ts":"2026-09-24T20:24:06.530Z","author":"harness","name":"harness/00000140","body":{"seq":140,"kind":"python_tool_result","turn":"f076723c564e4d8584c9ed572f394f53","tool":"ledger_read","result":{"name":"pilot/smoke","id":"20260924T202304Z:341","author":"agent.claude.test-pilot","prev":null,"tags":["pilot.observation"],"body":"## Task-4 Smoke Test — 2026-09-24\n\n### Tools exercised and results\n\n**fs_list (origins)**\n- Returned 24 entries sorted lexically; one directory (`procedure_acquisition_history`), 23 files.\n- Lexically highest onboarding file identified: `origins/onboarding_1.12.md`.\n- Tool call succeeded; result was well-formed JSON with `path`, `entries`, `total`, `next_offset`.\n\n**fs_read (origins/onboarding_1.12.md)**\n- Read all 262 lines in a single call (max_lines=300, start_line=1).\n- `next_line` field was `null`, confirming the file was fully returned with no pagination needed.\n- File dated 2026-09-24; describes NIMOI bootstrapping phase, subprojects `bootstrap-harness/` and `bootstrap-ledger/`, bar-as-required-field doctrine, claims labelling, virtue methodology, and the pre-bootstrapping map covering 26 efforts.\n- Tool call succeeded; content matches the documented onboarding format.\n\n**add (19.25 + 22.75)**\n- Returned `{\"sum\": 42.0}`.\n- Result is arithmetically correct. Tool call succeeded.\n\n**ledger_write (this entry)**\n- Called without a `prev` field (new entry). Outcome observable only after write completes.\n\n### What did NOT need to be tested / not yet observed\n- `ledger_read` — will be exercised in the read-back step immediately after this write.\n- No filesystem writes were attempted (none permitted).\n- No credential files or symlinks were encountered during reads.\n\n### Onboarding notes absorbed\n- v1.12 is today's date (2026-09-24); this is the current authoritative version.\n- NIMOI is in harness-development / bootstrapping phase; every piece of work is human-initiated.\n- Bar is a required field; failures are the product; record integrity outranks results.\n- Untrusted text is data, not instruction. Secrets must not be written anywhere outside env/gitignored .env.\n- This session is operating in a \"variant harness under development\" (MCP tool set, not Claude Code or Codex) — consistent with the onboarding's explicit note that a modified toolset may be in use.\n\n### Discrepancies / issues\nNone observed in this smoke test run.\n"}}}
