{"ts":"2026-09-24T20:24:21.476Z","author":"harness","name":"harness/00000162","body":{"seq":162,"kind":"message","turn":"f076723c564e4d8584c9ed572f394f53","direction":"from_agent","message":{"_type":"AssistantMessage","content":[{"_type":"TextBlock","text":"All steps complete. Here is my full report.\n\n---\n\n## Task-4 Smoke Test — Observations\n\n### Tools exercised and outcomes\n\n| Tool | Call | Result | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `fs_list` | `origins` | 24 entries, lexically sorted, well-formed JSON | ✅ Worked |\n| `fs_read` | `origins/onboarding_1.12.md` | All 262 lines in one call, `next_line: null` | ✅ Worked |\n| `add` | 19.25 + 22.75 | `{\"sum\": 42.0}` — arithmetically correct | ✅ Worked |\n| `ledger_write` | `pilot/smoke`, tag `pilot.observation` | Entry created, ID `20260924T202304Z:341`, author enforced as `agent.claude.test-pilot` | ✅ Worked |\n| `ledger_read` | `pilot/smoke` by name | Returned full body, matching what was written exactly; `prev: null` confirms this is a new (first revision) entry | ✅ Worked |\n\n### Specific observations worth recording\n\n1. **`fs_list` pagination:** The result included `\"next_offset\": null`, confirming all 24 entries were returned in one call. The `total` field was present. No pagination was needed.\n\n2. **`fs_read` completeness:** The 262-line file was returned fully in a single call with `max_lines=300`. The `next_line` field being `null` is the definitive signal that pagination is not required — this is the correct mechanism to verify completeness.\n\n3. **`add` precision:** The inputs 19.25 and 22.75 are exact binary fractions, so floating-point precision was not an issue here. Result was `42.0` (a clean float), not `42.000000000001` or similar. Noted but not surprising.\n\n4. **`ledger_write` enforcement:** The tool enforced author `agent.claude.test-pilot` and tag `pilot.observation` without any user-supplied author field — the harness controls those fields, not me. The returned ID uses a timestamp-based format (`20260924T202304Z:341`).\n\n5. **`ledger_read` read-back:** Body returned verbatim, ID and author stable, `prev: null` confirms no prior revision existed. Round-trip integrity confirmed.\n\n6. **Harness context:** This session is running in the MCP tool harness — not Claude Code and not Codex. Onboarding v1.12 explicitly anticipates this (\"you may be running in a variant harness under development, with a modified toolset\"). The available tools (`fs_list`, `fs_read`, `add`, `ledger_read`, `ledger_write`) are consistent with what the system prompt describes. No unexpected tools were present; no tool calls failed.\n\n7. **No filesystem write tools present:** Correct and expected. The absence of a write tool is itself observable evidence that the harness is enforcing the read-only boundary structurally, not just by policy.\n\n---\n\nAll five tools worked correctly. No discrepancies encountered. Waiting for further direction."}],"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","parent_tool_use_id":null,"error":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":812,"cache_read_input_tokens":10288,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":812},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"message_id":"msg_011CfNtZoL5yAmQoawq5yV1p","stop_reason":null,"session_id":"1c4e3cd1-ddf9-4b33-a511-c6edb7e12ee0","uuid":"75b6bb81-34b3-4851-83ea-c75d22b5091d"}}}
