e is consistent with this — it is Claude Code-based but with a modified toolset. My earlier inference was too strong; the correct description is that the *exposed tool surface* differs from a standard Claude Code session (no Bash, no file-write tool), not that the underlying runtime is unrelated. This correction is accepted and recorded.\\n\\n### Discrepancies / issues\\nNone. All tool calls either succeeded as expected or failed with clean, descriptive errors.\\n\"}"}],"error":null}}
